@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' The brand theme centres note bodies, which destroys the left column a list is read
' down. Scoped to notes, as _spec/internal/sbx/sbx-kit-contract.puml does.
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the two intents the egress layer exists for, and where the sbx backend carries neither
' covers: internal/egress/**
' covers: internal/sbx/**
' covers: internal/entrypoint/**
' covers: internal/workspace/mount.go
' covers: internal/runlog/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-entrypoint/main.go
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/contract/egress_vocabulary_test.go
' covers: tests/e2e/sbx_egress_test.go
' covers: tests/e2e/credentials_test.go
' covers: tests/e2e/sbx_test.go
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh
'
' Read with: _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml (I1 as designed),
' _spec/_paradigms/egress-boundary.puml (I2 as designed),
' _spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml + sbx-kit-contract.puml (the backend that moved),
' _spec/internal/dind/dind-sidecar.puml (the daemon question, in its original shape).
'
' ── AUTHORITATIVE SOURCES for everything claimed about sbx below ────────────
'   credentials + proxy injection : https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/security/credentials/
'   kit spec, credentials block   : https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/kits/
'   usage overview                : https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/
'   kit spec v2                   : https://github.com/docker/sbx-kits-contrib/blob/main/spec/SPEC-v2.md
'   Read from the CLI itself (v0.39.0): `sbx secret --help`, `sbx secret set --help`,
'   `sbx secret set-custom --help`, `sbx policy --help`, `sbx policy init --help`,
'   `sbx policy log --help`, `sbx policy check network --help`, `sbx run --help`.
'
' ── D1 · WHAT MAKES A WORKSPACE .env SAFE UNDER sbx — RESEARCH, NOT YET DECIDED
'
' 1. CURRENT STATUS (measured, not inferred)
'    * The /dev/null masks proveo lays over every .env* are DROPPED: sbx takes
'      directory workspaces only ("workspace path exists but is not a directory"),
'      and the repo directory carrying those same files is mounted regardless.
'    * The Kit's environment block carries no PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE, so inside the VM
'      the mode is "", ShouldSkipEnvLoad is false, and the prelude SOURCES the .env
'      with `set -a`. Every key in it becomes agent process environment.
'    * proveo writes <state>/<sid>/inject/broker.env — every provider.KeyVars() at
'      0600 — before the backend is chosen, and only the docker teardown removes it.
'      Measured on the dev host: 3 of 3 leftovers belonged to sbx sessions.
'    * The neutralize path makes E1+E2 sharper still: for a suppressed credential
'      proveo emits `-e VAR=` (empty) to override sbx's global store, so the agent
'      starts with an EMPTY key — and then the prelude sources the workspace .env
'      over it. Empty-then-filled is how a real key ends up in a variable proveo
'      deliberately blanked. (tests/e2e TestCredentialForwardingIntegrity asserts
'      the older contract — no provider key in argv at all — and fails at HEAD.)
'    * proveo pushes secrets with `sbx secret set --force <ENV_VAR_NAME>`, but sbx
'      keys its store on a SERVICE (anthropic, cursor, droid, github, google, groq,
'      mistral, nebius, openai, openrouter, xai). The dev host's store holds both
'      shapes side by side, and an OAuth entry for a service outranks an api-key one
'      at runtime — so what authenticates a run may be an entry proveo never named.
'
' 2. IDEAL sbx SETUP — the mechanism sbx ships, which IS proveo's broker, declared
'    "An HTTP/HTTPS proxy on your host intercepts outbound requests from the sandbox,
'     looks up the matching credential on the host, and overwrites the auth header
'     before forwarding." / "the real value never enters the sandbox — the agent sees
'     only a sentinel like `proxy-managed`."
'    * Storage is already a keychain: macOS Keychain, Windows Credential Manager,
'      Linux Secret Service, falling back to ~/.config/com.docker.sandboxes. proveo's
'      own plaintext broker.env is the outlier, not the keychain question.
'    * Kit `credentials[]` declares `apiKey.name`, `proxyManaged: true` and
'      `inject: [{domain, header, format}]` — names and headers only, never a value.
'      A mixin may NOT repeat a service the built-in agent declares ("defined in both").
'    * Values never ride argv: `sbx secret set` reads stdin; `--sandbox <name>` scopes
'      an entry to one sandbox instead of the global default.
'    * The value need not exist on disk at all: `--ref op://…` or an AWS Secrets
'      Manager ARN, or `--command 'gh auth token'`, with `--refresh` (default 55m, or
'      on-demand). "The secret store contains the reference or command instead of the
'      credential value."
'    * For a credential outside the closed service list: `sbx secret set-custom
'      --host <h> --env <VAR> --value …` places a generated PLACEHOLDER in the sandbox
'      and swaps it at the proxy.
'    * The docs answer the env-var question directly: "Set these to placeholder values
'      (e.g. `proxy-managed`) if needed. The proxy injects actual credentials
'      regardless of the environment variable value."
'
' 3. POSSIBLE SOLUTIONS (the open decision)
'    a. Publish the tier into the Kit — one line, restores the .env-load skip, leaves
'       the file readable to an agent that opens it itself.
'    b. Sentinel parity: inject `<VAR>=proxy-managed` on the sbx path the way the
'       docker path injects `proveo-brokered`, and let ApplyBrokerSentinel re-assert
'       it after any load. Closes the window (a) leaves, in sbx's own idiom.
'    c. Never hold the value: store `--ref`/`--command` sources, scope entries with
'       `--sandbox <sid>`, and stop writing inject/broker.env on this backend.
'    d. Refuse a run whose workspace .env holds a provider key unless
'       --credentials forward; or make --clone the sbx default so untracked files
'       never travel.
'    (b) + (c) together are the only combination that reproduces I1 as designed: the
'    agent holds a sentinel, the value lives in a keychain, and no plaintext copy
'    exists on the host or in the VM.
'
' ── DECIDED, AND LANDED IN THIS PASS ────────────────────────────────────────
'   D2 assert first — tests/e2e/sbx_egress_test.go probes direct egress AND a
'      container pull from inside the sandbox; `docker pull` succeeding against an
'      unallowlisted registry is what would prove the per-sandbox daemon is a path
'      around the Kit policy. It skips, loudly, on a host whose baseline allows all.
'   D3 record from sbx's own evidence — `sbx policy log <sandbox> --json` is captured
'      at teardown into <egDir>/sbx/policy-log.json, named in the transcript, and the
'      observability row is backend-aware instead of promising Squid logs.
'   D4 canonical-only boundary — open|allowlist|review are the only tier names an
'      in-container gate understands; broker/firewall/proxy stay CLI aliases that
'      egress.Canonical translates. Pinned by TestContainerBoundarySpeaksOnlyCanonical-
'      Tiers and TestBashPreludeNamesTheSameTiers, both proven to fail on a regression.
'
' ── D2, HALF-ANSWERED BY THE SUITE ITSELF ──────────────────────────────────
' tests/e2e TestEveryHarnessGetsTheDockerAccessItPromises FAILS at HEAD, on both
' sbx harnesses, with the probe reporting HAS-SOCKET and SERVER:29.7.2 inside the
' sandbox. assertSandboxReplacesDocker asserts the opposite — no socket, no daemon
' — which was true before the images took `com.docker.sandboxes.start-docker`. So
' the code and its own e2e now assert opposite things about one decision, and the
' daemon half of D2 is measured: a daemon IS reachable. What stays open is whether
' its containers escape the Kit allowlist, which needs a denying baseline —
' tests/e2e/sbx_egress_test.go probes exactly that and skips until then.
'
' Four more e2e assertions pin the retired HOME redirect (sbxHome deletes HOME and
' PROVEO_HOME on purpose and publishes PROVEO_STATE_HOME instead):
' TestProveoHomePersistence, TestSandboxKitIsAMixinCarryingNoCredentials,
' TestSandboxBackendCarriesProveoHomeBesideHome, and the claudecode entrypoint
' probe. All fail at pristine HEAD; all are the same drift this plan is about.
'
' ── THE MEASUREMENT THAT REFRAMES I2 ────────────────────────────────────────
' `sbx policy init <allow-all|balanced|deny-all>` fixes a GLOBAL baseline once per
' host, and Kit rules only ever ADD to it. On a host initialised allow-all the Kit's
' allowlist admits nothing extra and denies nothing. Measured on the dev host:
' `sbx policy check network proveo-egress-probe.invalid` answers Allowed; a sandbox
' whose Kit allowed `.anthropic.com` reached 22 distinct hosts (datadog intake, npm,
' pypi, sigstore, github); `blocked_hosts` was empty for every proveo sandbox.
' proveo now WARNS rather than printing a tier for a boundary that is not there.
title PLANNED — env + egress revision: two intents, and the backend that carries neither yet

frame "Why the layer exists — the two intents, stated once" as WHY <<host>> {
  component "**I1 · env safety**\nthe agent process never holds the real key,\nand cannot read one off the mounted tree" as I1 <<app>>
  component "**I2 · network safety + telemetry**\nno irreversible write, no leak to a third party —\nand every run leaves a record of what it reached" as I2 <<app>>
}

frame "docker + egress — how each intent is carried" as DOCK <<host>> {
  component "mask\n/dev/null over every .env* in the tree\n(workspace.maskEnvMounts)" as D_MASK <<app>>
  component "sentinel\n-e KEY=proveo-brokered · the real value\nreaches only the MITM's broker.env" as D_SENT <<app>>
  component "policy\nSquid ACL · read-allow / write-deny ·\nDLP header+body scan · CONNECT budget" as D_POL <<app>>
  component "record\nflows.ndjson + squid access.log,\ncaptured at teardown into the transcript" as D_REC <<app>>
}

frame "sbx — what the rendered Kit actually carries" as SBXF <<host>> {
  component "permissions.network.allow\nADDS to a host-wide baseline; narrows nothing\nwhen that baseline is allow-all" as S_ALLOW <<error>>
  component "sbx secret set (stdin, host-side)\nkeychain + proxy injection — sbx's own broker" as S_SEC <<app>>
  component "workspace = DIRECTORY binds only\nfile binds are dropped without a trace" as S_DIR <<error>>
  component "environment.variables\ncarries no PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE" as S_ENV <<error>>
}

frame "Gaps — I1, env safety" as GE <<host>> {
  component "E1 · the .env masks are dropped\nthe tree still carries the real files" as E1 <<error>>
  component "E2 · the prelude SOURCES that .env\nno mode ⇒ ShouldSkipEnvLoad is false" as E2 <<error>>
  component "E3 · the sentinel rewrite was dead\nboth preludes gated on mode == firewall" as E3 <<app>>
  component "E4 · Go and bash preludes disagreed\non which tiers skip the .env load" as E4 <<app>>
  component "E5 · inject/broker.env survives the run\nsbx teardown never removes that dir" as E5 <<error>>
  component "E6 · no warning fires either\nwarnMountedSecrets is open-tier only" as E6 <<error>>
  component "E7 · secrets stored by ENV VAR name\nsbx keys its store on a SERVICE" as E7 <<error>>
}

frame "Gaps — I2, network safety + telemetry" as GN <<host>> {
  component "N1 · the baseline decides, not the Kit\nallow-all host ⇒ nothing is confined" as N1 <<error>>
  component "N2 · no flow record, no per-run report" as N2 <<app>>
  component "N3 · the transcript promised Squid logs\nobservability() was not backend-aware" as N3 <<app>>
  component "N4 · a daemon in every sandbox\nstart-docker label, unconditional" as N4 <<error>>
}

frame "Why none of this went red" as T <<host>> {
  component "T1 · the .env e2e covers opencode only\nthe auth e2e sets PROVEO_SBX=off" as T1 <<error>>
  component "T2 · the sbx probe asserts liveness,\nmount write-through, docker, teardown" as T2 <<error>>
  component "T3 · entrypoint tests pinned firewall/proxy" as T3 <<app>>
  component "T4 · dind tests named no canonical tier" as T4 <<app>>
  component "T5 · Go↔bash parity covers bridges only" as T5 <<error>>
}

frame "Landed in this pass" as DONE <<host>> {
  component "canonical-only tier vocabulary\n+ two contract tests, proven to fail" as L1 <<app>>
  component "sbx policy log captured at teardown\n+ backend-aware observability row" as L2 <<app>>
  component "baseline preflight warning\nsaid before the posture, not after" as L3 <<app>>
  component "e2e: direct egress + daemon pull\nfrom inside a sandbox" as L4 <<app>>
}

frame "Still open" as DEC <<host>> {
  component "D1 · sentinel parity + keychain-only\ncredentials on the sbx path" as D1 <<async>>
  component "D2b · gate the per-sandbox daemon,\nonce the probe says whether it escapes" as D2 <<async>>
  component "D5 · own the baseline: refuse, narrow\nwith --deny-network, or accept" as D5 <<async>>
}

I1 ARROW_MAIN D_MASK
I1 ARROW_MAIN D_SENT
I2 ARROW_MAIN D_POL
I2 ARROW_MAIN D_REC

I1 ARROW_ERROR GE : not carried here
I2 ARROW_ERROR GN : not carried here

S_DIR ARROW_ERROR E1
S_ENV ARROW_ERROR E2
S_ALLOW ARROW_ERROR N1
S_SEC ARROW_OPTIONAL E7 : keyed on the wrong name

GE ARROW_QUEUE T : untested, so silent
GN ARROW_QUEUE T

T ARROW_QUEUE DONE
DONE ARROW_QUEUE DEC

note bottom of I1
  **Stated once because it was drifting.** The
  paradigms describe the docker rendering; the sbx
  one reads as a second design rather than one
  intent under a different enforcer. These two
  sentences are what a backend must satisfy.
end note

note bottom of D_MASK
  Applies on EVERY tier unless --credentials
  forward, so it is credential-shaped, not
  tier-shaped.
end note

note bottom of S_DIR
  "workspace path exists but is not a directory" —
  so every /dev/null mask is silently discarded,
  while the repo directory carrying those same
  files is mounted.
end note

note bottom of E2
  Measured on a rendered Kit: the environment
  block holds models, git identity, workdir, the
  MCP decline — and no tier. Inside, mode is "",
  which is not in the skip set, so the .env is
  read and its keys exported into the agent.
end note

note bottom of E3
  The tiers were renamed broker/firewall/proxy →
  open/allowlist/review and canonicalised
  host-side. Both gates still read the old name,
  so neither had fired since. Fixed in this pass;
  the vocabulary is now canonical-only.
end note

note bottom of E5
  Written before the backend is chosen, holding
  every provider key on the host at 0600, and
  removed only by the docker path's teardown.
  Measured on the dev host: 3 of 3 leftovers
  belong to sbx sessions.
end note

note bottom of N1
  The accepted gap was "no DLP on payloads to
  allowed hosts". The real one is wider: the
  global baseline decides, Kit rules only add, and
  on an allow-all host nothing is confined and
  nothing is blocked.
end note

note bottom of N4
  dind is gated behind five conditions because a
  reachable daemon is a path around the enforcer.
  sbx ships one per sandbox by image label. Do its
  containers inherit the Kit allowlist? The e2e
  probe answers it; the gate waits on that answer.
end note

note bottom of T1
  claudecode and cursor — the two harnesses that
  now take this backend — are absent from the .env
  suite, and the credential e2e sets PROVEO_SBX
  =off to reach docker. The property is
  asserted exactly where it already holds.
end note

note bottom of L2
  `sbx policy log <sandbox> --json` names allowed
  and blocked hosts, the matching rule, the proxy
  type and a request count. It is the sbx-side
  flows.ndjson, and the run keeps a copy the
  transcript points at.
end note

note bottom of D5
  `sbx run --deny-network` narrows one sandbox and
  "can only narrow, never widen". Whether proveo
  renders denies per run, demands a baseline, or
  states the truth and moves on is the decision
  this plan is waiting on.
end note
@enduml
